   "source": [
    "ctivation Function in Deep Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "An Activation Function decides whether a neuron should be activated (pass information forward) or not.\n",
    "\n",
    "Without an activation function, a neural network is just a series of linear calculations and cannot learn complex patterns.\n",
    "\n",
    "Why Do We Need Activation Functions?\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we have:\n",
    "\n",
    "y = wx + b\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a linear equation.\n",
    "\n",
    "Even if you stack 100 linear layers:\n",
    "\n",
    "Linear → Linear → Linear → Linear\n",
    "\n",
    "The result is still:\n",
    "\n",
    "One big Linear Function\n",
    "\n",
    "The network cannot learn:\n",
    "\n",
    "Images\n",
    "Speech\n",
    "Language\n",
    "Complex relationships\n",
    "\n",
    "Activation functions introduce non-linearity.\n",
    "\n",
    "Neural Network Flow\n",
    "Input\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Linear Layer\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Activation Function\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Linear Layer\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Activation Function\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Output\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "model = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "    nn.Linear(10, 5),\n",
    "    nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "    nn.Linear(5, 1)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "1. ReLU (Most Popular)\n",
    "nn.ReLU()\n",
    "\n",
    "Formula:\n",
    "\n",
    "f(x) = max(0, x)\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "Input\tOutput\n",
    "-5\t0\n",
    "-2\t0\n",
    "0\t0\n",
    "3\t3\n",
    "10\t10\n",
    "\n",
    "Graph:\n",
    "\n",
    "     /\n",
    "    /\n",
    "   /\n",
    "--/\n",
    "\n",
    "Advantages:\n",
    "\n",
    "Fast\n",
    "\n",
    "Simple\n",
    "\n",
    "Used in CNNs and Deep Networks\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Sigmoid\n",
    "\n",
    "Formula:\n",
    "\n",
    "f(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n",
    "\n",
    "Output Range:\n",
    "\n",
    "0 to 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "Input\tOutput\n",
    "-10\t0.000\n",
    "0\t0.5\n",
    "10\t0.999\n",
    "\n",
    "Graph:\n",
    "\n",
    "   ----\n",
    " /\n",
    "/\n",
    " \\\n",
    "  ----\n",
    "\n",
    "Used For:\n",
    "\n",
    "Binary Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "prob = torch.sigmoid(logits)\n",
    "\n",
    "Output:\n",
    "\n",
    "0.85 = 85% probability\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Tanh\n",
    "\n",
    "Formula:\n",
    "\n",
    "f(x)=tanh(x)\n",
    "\n",
    "Output Range:\n",
    "\n",
    "-1 to +1\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "Input\tOutput\n",
    "-5\t-1\n",
    "0\t0\n",
    "5\t1\n",
    "\n",
    "Used in:\n",
    "\n",
    "RNNs\n",
    "LSTMs\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Softmax\n",
    "\n",
    "Used in Multi-Class Classification.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "logits = [2.0, 1.0, 0.5]\n",
    "\n",
    "After Softmax:\n",
    "\n",
    "[0.63, 0.23, 0.14]\n",
    "\n",
    "Sum:\n",
    "\n",
    "0.63 + 0.23 + 0.14 = 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Used for:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cat\n",
    "Dog\n",
    "Horse\n",
    "\n",
    "Prediction:\n",
    "\n",
    "Highest Probability = Predicted Class\n",
    "5. Leaky ReLU\n",
    "\n",
    "Formula:\n",
    "\n",
    "f(x)=x          if x>0\n",
    "f(x)=0.01x      if x<0\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Input\tOutput\n",
    "-5\t-0.05\n",
    "5\t5\n",
    "\n",
    "Fixes:\n",
    "\n",
    "Dead ReLU Problem\n",
    "PyTorch Examples\n",
    "ReLU\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "\n",
    "relu = nn.ReLU()\n",
    "\n",
    "x = torch.tensor([-2., 3.])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(relu(x))\n",
    "\n",
    "Output:\n",
    "\n",
    "tensor([0., 3.])\n",
    "Sigmoid\n",
    "sigmoid = nn.Sigmoid()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(sigmoid(torch.tensor([0.])))\n",
    "\n",
    "Output:\n",
    "\n",
    "tensor([0.5000])\n",
    "Tanh\n",
    "tanh = nn.Tanh()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(tanh(torch.tensor([1.])))\n",
    "\n",
    "Output:\n",
    "\n",
    "tensor([0.7616])\n",
    "Which Activation Function to Use?\n",
    "Task\tActivation\n",
    "Hidden Layers\tReLU\n",
    "Binary Classification Output\tSigmoid\n",
    "Multi-Class Classification Output\tSoftmax\n",
    "RNN/LSTM\tTanh\n",
    "Deep Networks\tReLU / Leaky ReLU"
   ]
  }
 ],
